* cs01.hello - the first program: output, comments and the end of a program
*
* Every account has the example programs in its own file examples.bp, already compiled.  Run one where it is:
*    run examples.bp cs01.hello
* To change one, copy it to your bp file first (examples.bp is refreshed by an upgrade, so your change would not last there):
*    copy from examples.bp to bp cs01.hello
*    basic bp cs01.hello
*    run bp cs01.hello
*
* A line that begins with * is a comment: SD skips it.  So is anything after ;* on a line.
* crt writes to the terminal and ends the line; print does the same and can be sent to a printer.

program cs01.hello
   crt 'Hello, world!'
   crt 'This is SD BASIC.'           ;* a comment at the end of a line
   print 'One plus one is ' : 1 + 1  ;* : joins two values into one string
end
